<title>GERMANY: Daimler seeks to sell part of TEMIC - report.</title>
<headline>Daimler seeks to sell part of TEMIC - report.</headline>
<dateline>HAMBURG, Germany 1997-07-17</dateline>
<text>
<p>Daimler-Benz AG  is in talks to sell part of its stake in electronics unit TEMIC and TRW of the United States is considered a top candidate, Germany's &quot;Manager Magazin&quot; said on Thursday.</p>
<p>A Daimler spokesman said in response to a Reuter enquiry that a cooperation deal with an international partner for its TEMIC unit was possible but that no decision has been made.</p>
<p>He declined further comment.</p>
<p>The magazine said Daimler does not want to make a full divestment from TEMIC but remain as a minority partner.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
